 drawing to just completely  winning for me  in the span of a couple moves  but i was very fortunate to come away  from this game with a win  uh protecting my rating even the draw in  this game would have uh done some damage  to my rating given my opponent was over  800 points  low rated than me  so yeah the crucial moment was this  position  uh queen g6 turns out to be the only  move for black to hold equality because  d6 is a very big threat  and i've noticed this sometimes that  especially amateur level play  when a player delivers discover check  it's sometimes easy to overlook the fact  that  it's not the piece moving that's doing  the checking  it's a piece being unleashed so it's  possible my opponent just missed my  chance to play d6  and i was very fortunate that turned  into a winning position  so just to show here if my opponent  blockaded the pawn  i would happily take go up upon  queen d5 coming and uh it still takes  some work to convert but this would  still be winning for white  um so that's about it for game seven  played the london could have gotten  advantage out of the  kind of mid to late middle game  uh opponent played really really well to  not only neutralize my my play  but outplay me at some point i was  probably worse at some point in this  game  and uh okay i walked away with a win  this put me at five and a half out of  seven in the standings with two more  games to go  so this time i'm not lying  next game will feature a staffer gambit  stay tuned it'll be a fun one  don't forget to like and subscribe  as always if you have questions  leave them in the comments below and  i'll see you in the next video
 

